<article class="env-lemma" id="09BP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09BP">Lemma <span data-tag="09BP">61.26.6</span>.</a> Let $j : U \to X$ be a quasi-compact open immersion morphism of schemes. The functor $j_! : \textit{Ab}(U_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}) \to \textit{Ab}(X_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale})$ commutes with limits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $j_!$ is exact it suffices to show that $j_!$ commutes with products. The question is local on $X$, hence we may assume $X$ affine. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be an abelian sheaf on $U_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}$. We have $j^{-1}j_*\mathcal{G} = \mathcal{G}$. Hence applying the exact sequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/09AH" data-tag="09AH">61.26.5</a> we get 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to j_!\mathcal{G} \to j_*\mathcal{G} \to i_*i^{-1}j_*\mathcal{G} \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $i : Z \to X$ is the inclusion of the reduced induced scheme structure on the complement $Z = X \setminus U$. The functors $j_*$ and $i_*$ commute with products as right adjoints. The functor $i^{-1}$ commutes with products by Lemma <a href="/tag/09AA" data-tag="09AA">61.25.3</a>. Hence $j_!$ does because on the pro-étale site products are exact (Cohomology on Sites, Proposition <a href="/tag/0947" data-tag="0947">21.51.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>